-- title:
--   Unramifiedness at non-maximal primes of the X₁(Mp) chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Inside the Laurent series field $L((q))$ let $K$ be the intermediate field over $L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$, of the $q$-expansion field $\operatorname{adjoin}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, and let $K_1$ be the corresponding field for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, with $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, and equip $K$ and $K_1$ with $A$-algebra structures compatible with $L$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose images in $L((q))$ are both the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series})$ of $j$. Write $B = \operatorname{chartAlgFin} A\,K\,j$ and $B_1 = \operatorname{chartAlgFin} A\,K_1\,j_1$ for the subalgebras of elements integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j_1]$, and let $\iota_F : B_1 \to B$ be an $A$-algebra map compatible with the inclusions into $L((q))$. Then, with $B$ regarded as a $B_1$-algebra via $\iota_F$, for every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ that is not maximal, $B$ is unramified over $B_1$ at $Q$.
--
--   This is the ramification computation for the two-chart integral model of the covering $X_1(Mp) \to X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: the assertion covers the generic point and the height-one primes (closed points of the generic fibre and generic points of the components of the special fibre), and says nothing about the closed points of the special fibre. It feeds the construction of the stalk data at the finite chart used later in the analysis of this model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isUnramifiedAt_chartAlgFin_of_not_isMaximal_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul_x1x0.lean

